 ## Overview
-The Mixture Graph is a data structure for compressing, rendering, and querying segmentation histograms derived from volumetric segment ID data [S1]. It solves the problem of efficiently handling the high dimensionality and storage requirements of hierarchical histograms by factorizing normalized mixture vectors into a directed acyclic graph (DAG) of linear interpolations [S1]. Unlike traditional paletted textures where the palette is static, the Mixture Graph’s palette stores mixtures of multiple colors and is updated efficiently in parallel, allowing for pre-filtered anti-aliasing and interactive rendering [S1, S6].
