 ### Normalized Histogram Mipmap
-A hierarchical segmentation histogram $H$ constructed from a volume of segment IDs $S$. It stores mixtures (convex combinations of segment IDs) at multiple resolution levels. It uses the traditional average-of-eight mipmap filter, but other low-pass filters can be used if they can be normalized to a mixture [S1].
+A hierarchical segmentation histogram $H$ constructed from a volume of segment IDs $S$ [S1]. It stores mixtures (convex combinations of segment IDs) at multiple resolution levels [S1]. It uses the traditional average-of-eight mipmap filter, but other low-pass filters can be used if they can be normalized to a mixture [S1].
 
 ### Mixture Lookup Table for Range Queries
-A lookup table assembled on the CPU for range queries. Each node stores two sparse vectors over $\mathbb{R}^\infty$: the expected value $\mu$ and its variance $\delta\mu$. Build time depends on the number of nodes, topological depth, initial number of segments, and number of non-zero entries. For example, the Neocortex lookup table size is around 251MB [S1].
